## Decisions

### Beyond an activity’s invitation, should invited-only guests receive its Loop mail and count in groups whose rules use that activity?

The activity guest/volunteer separation is implemented and tested. The remaining review raises a broader membership choice. Previously, adding a guest also made them a volunteer, so guests already received the activity’s Loop mail and entered groups built from that activity. The new invitation state preserves that reach while removing the volunteer commitment. I initially planned to filter it, then checked the old code and found this was existing behavior; I have not changed propagation.

**Real production example, verified with queries:**
- **Staff Birthdays** permits its members to post and reply to its Loop mailing list.
- **Birthdays Viewers** is a group whose rule includes Staff Birthdays’ effective members.
- The **Birthdays app** grants access to Birthdays Viewers.

**Same input for every choice:** a host invites a guest to the real Staff Birthdays activity without a volunteer sign-up. Assume this guest has no other route to Birthdays app access. All choices keep that guest out of HCA-Team’s volunteer count and capacity, and taking them off sends no volunteer-cancellation mail.

- (*) Guest list and Loop
  The guest gets the Staff Birthdays invitation and Loop messages, and may post/reply there. The invitation does **not** put them in Birthdays Viewers, so it grants no Birthdays app access. Signing up as a volunteer later makes them qualify for that rule. I recommend this because it keeps guests in the activity’s conversation while separating invitations from membership in other groups.
- ( ) Guest list only
  The guest gets invitations and reminders, but no Staff Birthdays Loop messages or member posting/replying rights. They do not enter Birthdays Viewers or gain Birthdays app access. A volunteer sign-up grants those memberships later; guests stay outside the activity’s general email conversation until then.
- ( ) Keep existing membership reach
  The guest gets invitations and Loop messages, may post/reply, enters Birthdays Viewers and can open the Birthdays app before volunteering. This preserves the existing mailing and group-membership model; inviting someone also grants the access carried by rules using that activity.

<details><summary>Other affected production groups and verification</summary>
Five plain groups derive membership from activities: International Night, Spelling Bee, Spelling Bee Spellers, MS Halloween and Birthdays Viewers. Some rules also include students’ parents, so the same decision determines whether an invited family enters those parent mailing lists.

The core feature has focused database tests, vet, independent peer checks and browser checks. The production invitation column is already created. No existing volunteer sign-ups need migration. The full database suite exceeded its required 30-second cap; the focused suites pass.
